.TH CYVIEW 1 "December 2025" "cyview" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cyview \- view Cytoscape.js JSON graphs (.cyjs) with a lightweight local web viewer

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cyview
.RI [ options ] " FILE.cyjs"
.PP
.B cyview
.RI [ options ] " \-"
.PP
.I producer
| \fBcyview\fR [options]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcyview\fR is a small Linux command that opens an interactive viewer for Cytoscape.js JSON graphs (commonly stored with the \fI.cyjs\fR extension).
It runs a tiny local HTTP server and opens a browser window (preferably Chromium in app mode) to display the diagram.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-ui " {auto|chromium|xdg-open|print-url}"
Select how the viewer is opened.

.TP
.BR \-\-styles " NAME"
Select a style scheme. The scheme controls which \fBcyview.styles\fR file name is searched and applied.
If not specified, \fBcyview\fR uses the environment variable \fBCYVIEW_STYLES\fR if set; otherwise it uses \fBdefault\fR.

Special value:
.RS
.TP
.B list
Print discovered scheme names (one per line) and exit. This is useful for shell tab completion.
.RE

.TP
.BR \-\-bind " ADDR"
Bind address for the local HTTP server.

.TP
.BR \-\-port " PORT"
Port for the local HTTP server.

.TP
.BR \-\-once
Exit after the viewer page (\fIviewer.html\fR) is served the first time (best-effort).

.TP
.BR \-\-emit " json"
Emit machine-readable information to stdout.

.TP
.BR \-\-keep-alive
In Chromium mode, do not auto-exit when Chromium closes (debugging).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CYVIEW_STYLES
Default style scheme name to use when \fB--styles\fR is not provided.

.SH STYLES CONFIGURATION
(See previous version of this man page content; the scheme naming, replace semantics, merge semantics, and search order are unchanged.)
.PP
Scheme naming:
.IP \(bu 2
Scheme \fBdefault\fR uses \fBcyview.styles\fR
.IP \(bu 2
Any other scheme name \fBNAME\fR uses \fBcyview.styles.NAME\fR

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1),
.BR chromium (1)
